course: dictionary
lesson: 14243
title: Necktie and tie
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A necktie is a long, narrow piece of cloth that you wear round your neck, under your shirt collar. You tie it in a knot at the front. The clues are in the words around it.
explain: «Mum helped me tie my striped necktie before the school photo.» The word tie here is a verb, an action: to make a knot. The necktie is the thing you wear.
explain: In the UK and Australia, people usually say «tie» for the same thing. If you read a North American book and meet necktie, look at the clues: around the neck, under the collar, a knot at the front. Those clues show you what it means.
fact: A necktie is a long, narrow piece of cloth worn round the neck, under a shirt collar.
fact: A necktie is tied in a knot at the front.
fact: In the UK and Australia, most people say «tie» for the same thing.
fact: «Necktie» is mostly used in North America, and it sounds a little old-fashioned to many people elsewhere.
fact: Many school uniforms include a tie.
exercise: «Ravi tied his striped necktie in a neat knot before the school photo.» What is a necktie? | A hat worn in the sun | *A long, narrow piece of cloth worn round the neck | A small bag for pencils
exercise: Our school uniform needs a white shirt, grey trousers and a navy necktie. Where is a necktie worn? | Round the wrist | On the head | *Round the neck, under the shirt collar
exercise: In the UK, people often say «tie» for the same thing as a necktie. Which word means the same? | Button | Collar | *Tie | Scarf
test: Where do you tie a necktie? | On your belt | *At the front of your neck, in a knot | On your ankle | Around your wrist
test: Which word means a necktie in the UK? | Sock | Glove | *Tie | Belt
exam: «Grandad put on his best suit and tied a bright red necktie.» What does necktie most likely name? | A type of bread | *Something worn round the neck and tied in a knot | A small boat | A kind of shoe
